# Component Conventions

## General Rules

- Functional components only; no class components
- Always annotate return type: `function Foo(): ReactElement`
- Default exports for pages and layout; named exports are fine for small utilities
- No prop drilling beyond one level — use the `data/` layer or a hook

## Reusable UI Components

Before writing custom button/link/wrapper markup, check `src/components/ui/` first.

**Button** — use for all CTA interactions:
```tsx
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button'

// as a button
<Button variant="primary" size="lg" onClick={handleClick}>Get the App</Button>

// as an anchor link
<Button as="a" href="https://..." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Subscribe</Button>
```
Variants: `primary` (pink), `secondary` (glass), `ghost` (text-only)
Sizes: `sm`, `md`, `lg`

**Container** — wraps page content with max-width and horizontal padding:
```tsx
import Container from '@/components/ui/Container'

<Container size="lg">…content…</Container>
```
Sizes: `sm` (2xl), `md` (4xl), `lg` (6xl), `xl` (7xl)

## Page Components

Pages are thin — they contain layout/structure and delegate to components. They do not contain:
- Hardcoded data (use `src/data/`)
- Fetch logic (use `src/hooks/`)

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — page imports data and hooks
import { PLANS } from '@/data/pricing'
import { useReleases } from '@/hooks/useReleases'

// ❌ BAD — data hardcoded in page
const PLANS = [{ name: 'Basic', price: 25, ... }]
```

## Data Layer

All site content that might change or be reused lives in `src/data/`:

- **`navigation.ts`** — add items to `NAV_LINKS` to auto-populate header + footer
- **`social.ts`** — `SOCIAL_LINKS` and `CONTACT_EMAIL`; both header and footer read from here
- **`pricing.ts`** — plan definitions, Stripe checkout links, currency detection

## Hooks

Async/stateful logic belongs in `src/hooks/`. Each hook file exports a single `useFoo` function.

## HubSpot Forms

Two forms are embedded via `data-form-id` attributes on a `div.hs-form-frame`:
- **Try Now modal**: form-id `e7b7312c-1884-4467-a616-42a27512a402` (via `TryNowModal`)
- **Newsletter**: form-id `98567906-bbd8-4dde-99f6-4581261e62cf`

Both use portal `146425863`, region `eu1`. Load the HubSpot script (`https://js-eu1.hsforms.net/forms/embed/146425863.js`) once via a `useEffect` with a guard against duplicate injection.
